  "limitations": [
    "Independent implementations are offline qualification fixtures, not shipped vendor integrations. No SDK, credential, external call or live delivery is added. Default factories and the executable local composition remain mock-only.",
    "Integration tests inject adapters at existing infrastructure composition seams. They do not establish a supported live runtime profile or enable real mode through settings. Future provider composition requires separate review and explicit network/credential policy.",
    "Durable-receipt capability metadata is a composition declaration, never approval authority. The unchanged application dispatcher still requires exact authorization and a matching persisted receipt; a remote effect and local receipt are not atomic.",
    "The dependency-free connection witness is a static bridge-architecture assertion, not behavioral proof. Contract and migrated-database integration gates provide the separate behavior evidence. Live provider idempotency, rate limits, cancellation and uncertain-outcome reconciliation still require vendor-specific qualification.",
    "CI remains disabled. No remote branch publication or final whole-system acceptance is claimed by this requirement."
  ]
